# docs/USAGE.md's examples, one row an image: <flag>|<example>|<setup>
#
# <flag> is a row of common/flags, and every row there needs one here: the
# docs prettier plugin (.github/prettier-plugin-docs.mjs) writes USAGE.md's
# _Every command_ from both files and fails on a flag either one lacks.
# Rows print in common/flags' order; a flag's own rows in this file's.
# <example> is the words after the flag, one space apart (no quoting, no
# expansion); empty runs the bare flag, and `-` shows no image - a connect
# modifier, or a command whose output is the network's.
# <setup> is a hi command run first, unseen, in the same throwaway home.
# docs/tapes/usage.sh renders each example as usage-<flag>[-<n>].svg, <n>
# counting a flag's second row and on.
--help||
--version||
--use|-|
--plain|-|
--mux|-|
--no-mux|-|
--keep|-|
--no-keep|-|
--end|-|
--preview|colors|
--preview|packages|
--preview|header|
--doctor|--problems|--install --yes --link user
--install|--yes --dry-run|
--uninstall|--dry-run|--install --yes --link user
--configure|--preset minimal --dry-run|
--update|-|
--add-package|useful lazygit,tig --dry-run|
--remove-package|kubectl --dry-run|
--add-tag|web-dev dev --dry-run|
--set-color|hosttag prod red --dry-run|
--unset-color|username root --dry-run|
--plugins||--plugin-off mux
--plugin-off|prompt --dry-run|
--plugin-on|mux --dry-run|--plugin-off mux
--add-plugin|cli lnav/config.json lnav - ~/.config/lnav/config.json --dry-run|
--remove-plugin|lnav/config.json --dry-run|--add-plugin cli lnav/config.json lnav - ~/.config/lnav/config.json
